A .ssl script whose content is a one-line SQL statement. SQL-mode
classification is scoped to data sources (feature.diagnostics_pipeline
A12, feature.formatting A11), so this stays SSL: the SSL checks run and
report on the SQL syntax, and the formatter treats it as SSL that does
not parse, so the line is left as written, with no `;` added (issue #351;
formatting/semicolons/unparsed_sql_lines covers the multi-line form). The
flag variants run the same content under `--ds`, which declares any input
a data source (feature.cli_contract A15): then it is SQL, passes through
unchanged and reports nothing.
-- input.ssl --
select v.vendor_id from vendor v where v.active = 'Y' and v.region = 'EU'
-- format [--ds] --
select v.vendor_id from vendor v where v.active = 'Y' and v.region = 'EU'
-- diagnostics [--ds] --
-- format --
select v.vendor_id from vendor v where v.active = 'Y' and v.region = 'EU'
